{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1:000047:note_appended:bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1:85b8a8e782c0f34bee89b802ea875e270329d994dc862e026cb0e8017a931d6e","timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:01:25Z","actor":"bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1.land","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Land audit at 0e6b0400 (follow-up triage): none of the five child phases recorded a PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP note, so no /sase_new_task filing was needed. The parent phase's note #2 (annotated-overwrite archive moves issue no didMoveToURL) predates this epic and says the batch-15 lander should decide; it is left to that lander. Native macOS verification is still unavailable (ssh mac timed out again on 2026-10-27), so the Mac move-fixture run, the Mac app bundle/typecheck, and real Highlights acceptance stay recorded limitations, not new tasks. Epic-caused leftover to finish before close: phase 2 left the old uncoordinated rename path (apply_and_verify/apply_transaction/rollback_applied/write_id_marker using MarkerWriteSession::uncoordinated) as dead code. The module-wide #[allow(dead_code)] on highlights_ref::rename hides it. There is also a stale allow on coordinate_explicit_pdf_move_with and a no-op block in rollback_inside_move_scope. No commits landed on master after the epic started, so no integration was needed. No epic-symbol entries for the epic or its parent phase."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1:000048:note_appended:bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1:87664c46927a1da8296b39af67282c498bbacc9227f1d688097fb514c6112b66","timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:18:58Z","actor":"bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1.land","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-an.6.6.6.5.6.5.5.6.6.6.6.6.6.6.2.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Land audit: all five phases verified in source at bob-cli 0e6b0400 (phase 1 f00ae66e move-coordination scope; phase 2 1e923594 rename+id-repair as one coordinated transaction; phase 3 22882a7d guarded publish boundary in highlights_ref/publish.rs; phase 4 0971ad56 capture writers on that boundary; phase 5 0e6b0400 docs plus acceptance kit, Bob Refs hint removed). Mac commit 9db33a6 removed quietHint and added retry-draft tests. No post-epic drift on master to integrate. No epic-symbol entries for the epic or its parent phase.\n\nThis tale's cleanup (bob-cli working tree): deleted the legacy uncoordinated rename path in src/native/highlights_ref/rename/plan.rs (apply_and_verify, apply_transaction, rollback_applied, write_id_marker, plus the forced_verify_failure_reverses_moves_and_restores_rewrites test that only exercised it). Production goes execute_rename_with_session -> rename_move_accessor/rename_merge_accessor -> write_id_marker_with_saved. Removed the no-op block in rollback_inside_move_scope and the now write-only AppliedRename.moves field (extend line and transaction_for_rollback literal). Fixed the phase-2 clippy lints without behavior or message changes (matches! merge of the three retry hints; dropped to_path_buf; let-chain collapses in commit_inside_scope, rollback_inside_move_scope, rename_merge_accessor). Removed the dead-code allows on highlights_ref::rename and coordinate_explicit_pdf_move_with; MarkerWriteSession::uncoordinated() is now #[cfg(test)] with its only caller the marker_write test. Removing the module allow surfaced no other dead item. No docs/CLI/version/CHANGELOG/memory edits; bob-plugins and bob-mac-capture untouched.\n\nVerification (all on this tree): cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D unused -A unused_extern_crates -A unused_macro_rules -D private_interfaces exit 0 (remaining warnings pre-date the epic, none in the touched files); cargo test --lib highlights_ref::rename 30 passed; cargo test --lib marker_write 20 passed; cargo test --lib publish 30 passed; cargo test --test cli ref_library::rename 15 passed; just check exit 0 (includes fmt plus the full suite).\n\nFollow-up triage: no child phase recorded a PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP, so no task beads filed. Parent phase note #2 (archive moves issue no didMoveToURL) is left to the batch-15 lander, as that note asks.\n\nNative limitations: the Mac was offline (ssh mac timed out), so the macOS NSDocument move-fixture run, the disposable Mac Scripts/bundle.sh / just typecheck-tests, and real Highlights acceptance were not run. Linux portable tests, just portable-check via just check, and the acceptance kit --self-test passed during the phases."}}
